{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner steering at 20:45 Eastern on builder's finding 1b5b048f under b8c5a3c8, within the request. The two required-check gaps are closed by making the reservation the check's origin and the host's staging area, which is what \"the tree is built at reserve\" means in full: (1) at reserve the destination builds the integration commit from the manifest list, records in the reservation the base head, the tree, the paths with digests and the integration commit id, and stages that commit on the canonical Git host under a reservation ref (refs/artroom/reservations/\u003creservation id\u003e) before any check runs; publication later moves the branch head to it and the reservation ref is cleaned up as the receipt's tokens are today; (2) the checker service's origin reads base, tree and integration from the reservation (packages/checkers/src/job.ts), not from the manifest entry's effects, for both the one-file and the list manifest, so originOf answers for both; the runner fetches the integration commit from the reservation ref. A reservation without a staged commit, or a staged commit whose tree differs from the recorded tree, is refused by name and the check does not run. Tests on real scopes: the two-file reservation's commit fetched by the runner from the reservation ref, the configured check passing on it and publication following; the mismatch refusal as a control. No pack, no new user act, no legacy pin change. The deadline stands: filed for review by Saturday 12:00 Eastern.","body":{"decision":"reservation-as-check-origin-and-staging"}}